# Retrieval queries with content anchors (rq-01 ... rq-26).
# Labels are short verbatim quotes from evals/raw_docs, never chunk ids: chunk
# ids point at different text as soon as --chunk-size/--overlap changes.
# resolve_relevant_chunks() raises when an anchor matches nothing, so a rebuild
# with a much larger chunk size fails loudly instead of scoring zero.
#
# type: direct | paraphrase | distractor | cross_chunk
# A query with two anchors expects several relevant chunks (cross-chunk recall).
{"id": "rq-01", "type": "direct", "query": "pgvector 里 HNSW 索引的 m 参数默认是多少，调大有什么代价", "relevant_anchors": ["the max number of connections per layer"], "notes": "single fact in the HNSW index options list"}
